WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:11.800
Build every RAG prompt the same way: stable ids, sources first, question last, rules for sources only, conflicts, abstention, and untrusted content.

3
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:21.915
Prefer the provider’s citation mechanism when it exists, because it is cheaper and its pointers are guaranteed, and keep a prompt-based format for providers without one.

4
00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:27.891
Verify provenance and fidelity in code on every answer, against the cited passage only.

5
00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:30.005
Log enough to check support later.

6
00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:37.304
Then remember what the checks can’t see: a stale source quoted perfectly, and a real quote that doesn’t support its claim.

7
00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:42.896
The next lesson is about those failures, and about the cases where the right answer is “I don’t know.

8
00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:43.474
”.
